![major](https://app.cortex.foundation/badges/security/major.svg) **Duplicate yield of data and onSseEvent callback**

For each parsed event, the code calls onSseEvent (line 206) and then yields the data (line 214). This means downstream consumers iterating the async generator will see the same event twice: once via the callback and once via the yield, which is likely unintended and breaks the contract that the generator is the primary data source.

```suggestion
if (dataLines.length) {
                yield data as any;
              } else {
                onSseEvent?.({
                  data,
                  event: eventName,
                  id: lastEventId,
                  retry: retryDelay,
                });
              }
```

