![blocking](https://app.cortex.foundation/badges/security/blocking.svg) **getParseAs returns undefined implicitly when cleanContent is empty**

When the content type is a valid string that, after splitting on ';' and trimming, becomes empty (e.g., ';' or 'text/plain;' becomes ''), the function returns an implicit `undefined`. Its declared return type `Exclude<Config['parseAs'], 'auto'>` does not include `undefined`, so a caller that uses the return value without checking for `undefined` may get unexpected behavior or a type error at runtime. The previous line returned early for null/undefined, but not for empty string after trimming.

```suggestion
if (!cleanContent) {
    return 'stream';
  }
```

